---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/Hero.astro';
import Section from '../../components/Section.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Trains and Castles Resources for Parents, Teachers, and Libraries"
  description="Resources for parents, teachers, and libraries using Trains and Castles, including comic companion chapters and printable coloring pages for young readers."
>
  <Hero
    title="Trains and Castles Resources"
    subtitle="For parents, teachers, libraries, and young readers."
    text="Trains and Castles is a children's companion book about travel, imagination, curiosity, and wonder. It follows a young reader's journey through trains, castles, cities, and quiet moments of discovery."
    primaryHref="#companion-materials"
    primaryLabel="Explore Materials"
    secondaryHref="/trains-and-castles"
    secondaryLabel="About the Book"
  />

  <Section>
    <div class="intro-panel">
      <p>
        This site now includes public companion materials for <em>Trains and Castles</em>:
        comic-style chapters to read and printable coloring pages to use at home, in
        classrooms, or in library settings.
      </p>
      <p>
        The materials are meant to extend the book gently, giving young readers more ways
        to spend time with the journey without turning it into a hard sell or a formal program.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Who this is for">
    <div class="resource-audience-grid">
      <article class="card resource-card">
        <h2>For Parents</h2>
        <p>
          Use the book as a quiet family reading experience, a travel-inspired bedtime story,
          or a way to extend a child's curiosity about trains, castles, places, and memory.
        </p>
        <p>
          The comics and printable coloring pages can support screen-light activities,
          conversation starters, and a simple way to keep the story close after reading.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="card resource-card">
        <h2>For Teachers</h2>
        <p>
          Teachers can use the story and companion materials to support reading, discussion,
          drawing, sequencing, storytelling, and place-based curiosity.
        </p>
        <p>
          The comic chapters offer a visual storytelling extension, while coloring pages give
          students a calm, printable way to respond to scenes and ideas from the book.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="card resource-card">
        <h2>For Libraries</h2>
        <p>
          Libraries can share the book with families, young readers, and local-author
          audiences, while the companion comics and coloring pages create simple ways to
          extend the experience.
        </p>
        <p>
          The printable pages can fit naturally with children's collection discovery,
          family reading, activity tables, or quiet passive programming.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Companion Materials" className="resources-materials-section">
    <div id="companion-materials" class="grid two-up">
      <article class="card resource-card">
        <h2>Read the Comics</h2>
        <p>
          Explore comic-style companion chapters inspired by the book, organized by chapter
          with local page previews and whole-chapter PDF downloads.
        </p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/trains-and-castles/comics">Read the Comics</a>
      </article>

      <article class="card resource-card">
        <h2>Printable Coloring Pages</h2>
        <p>
          Print coloring pages for young readers, families, teachers, and libraries, with
          individual view and download links for each page.
        </p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/trains-and-castles/coloring-pages">Explore Coloring Pages</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section title="More from the Journey">
    <div class="resource-audience-grid">
      <article class="card resource-card">
        <h2>Bonus Reflections</h2>
        <p>
          Read small companion reflections that did not belong on the printed page
          but still belong to the journey.
        </p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/bonus">Read Bonus Reflections</a>
      </article>

      <article class="card resource-card">
        <h2>How the Books Were Made</h2>
        <p>
          See how the travel story, comic chapters, and coloring pages came together
          from the same shared experience.
        </p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/process">Explore the Process</a>
      </article>

      <article class="card resource-card">
        <h2>Photos from the Journey</h2>
        <p>
          Browse chapter-based photos that preserve the places, details, and moments
          behind the books.
        </p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/photos">View Photos</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Books">
    <p>
      Explore the related books in this small publishing ecosystem without adding
      full-book downloads or new products.
    </p>
    <a class="button button-secondary" href="/books">View Books</a>
  </Section>

  <Section title="About the book">
    <p>
      <em>Trains and Castles</em> follows the same journey as <em>The Tracks Remember</em>,
      but through the eyes of a child. It is built around travel, curiosity, and the wonder
      of seeing unfamiliar places for the first time.
    </p>
    <a class="button" href="/trains-and-castles">Learn More About the Book</a>
    <a
      class="button button-secondary"
      href="https://a.co/d/08TJjA3Z"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"
    >
      View on Amazon
    </a>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>
